    "Report the shift as positive when the sample peaks sit at higher wavenumbers than the reference, i.e. the value you subtract to correct them."
    If $x_{sample} = x_{ref} + \text{shift}$, then $\text{shift} > 0$ means sample is shifted right (higher wavenumbers).
